  "label": "User projected onto the baseball player as the one transitioning from catcher to pitcher",
  "description": "The user is implicitly projected onto the baseball player (visual material) holding the catcher's mitt, as the text 'the day you graduate from catcher to pitcher' uses 'you' to address the viewer, making the viewer the subject of the metaphorical transition. The player's posture and the text create a direct identification with the user as the one undergoing this role change.",
